@startuml
title Expense Track - Application and Database Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Member / Admin" as User

node "Client Device" {
  component "Web Browser" as Browser
}

node "Django Web Server" {
  component "URL Routes\nconfig/urls.py" as Routes
  component "Authentication\nDjango auth + forms" as Auth
  component "Expenses Features\nviews + models" as Expenses
  component "Templates + Static Files" as Templates
}

database "PostgreSQL Production Database" as PostgreSQL {
  component "Authentication Tables\nUsers and Sessions" as AuthTables
  component "Expense Tables\nTransactions, Budgets, Goals" as ExpenseTables
}

cloud "Email Provider\n(password reset)" as Email

User --> Browser
Browser --> Routes : HTTPS requests
Routes --> Auth : signup, login,\nlogout, reset
Routes --> Expenses : dashboard and CRUD
Routes --> Templates : render HTML
Auth --> AuthTables : users and sessions
Expenses --> ExpenseTables : user-owned data
Expenses --> AuthTables : owner foreign key
Auth --> Email : password-reset email

note right of PostgreSQL
Local development may use SQLite.
Production uses DATABASE_URL
to connect to PostgreSQL.
end note

@enduml
